whisper: Options typed after a program's name, like:  stellanova tool.stella --size=3 --loud notes.txt
whisper: Written in Stellanova itself. Use it in a program with:  use: options.stella
whisper: An option is "--name" or "--name=value". Every word after "--" on its own is a plain word.

to option at, given name (text), returning a number:
  set words to the words given
  for each n from 1 to the size of words:
    if item n of words is "--": return 0
    if item n of words is "--" plus name or item n of words begins with "--" plus name plus "=": return n
  return 0
and the universe said i love you

to has option, given name (text), returning yes or no:
  return option at name exceeds 0
and the universe said i love you

to option value, given name (text) and fallback (text, usually ""), returning text:
  set n to option at name
  if n is 0: return fallback
  set word to item n of the words given
  if word is "--" plus name: return fallback
  return letters ((the size of name) plus 4) to (the size of word) of word
and the universe said i love you

to plain words, returning a list of text:
  set found to a list of text
  set rest to no
  for each word in the words given:
    if rest or not (word begins with "--"):
      add word to found
    otherwise if word is "--":
      set rest to yes
  return found
and the universe said i love you
